<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!--
        The dark counterpart of `values/themes.xml`, which did not exist.

        The app declared one theme, `Material.Light`, in every configuration, so
        `android:windowBackground` was light even on a device in dark mode. That
        showed as a white flash on every page change, in the frames where a
        NavHost transition has faded one screen out and not yet faded the next
        one in.

        The transition itself is fixed in `MainActivity`, which now paints an
        opaque `surface` under the graph and is correct whatever `ThemePreference`
        resolves to. This file covers the frames before Compose draws at all: the
        cold start, where only the window background exists.

        It follows the system rather than the in-app setting, because a resource
        qualifier cannot see `ThemePreference`. Forcing Dark from Settings on a
        light system still opens on a light frame; that is a launch flash rather
        than a navigation one, and fixing it means painting the window at runtime.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.Focuslist" parent="android:Theme.Material.NoActionBar" />
</resources>
